@startuml
' ResumeGPT data model — mirrors prisma/schema.prisma
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
hide circle
hide empty members

title ResumeGPT — Data Model

class User {
  +id : String <<PK>>
  +username : String <<unique>>
  +createdAt : DateTime
}

class Project {
  +id : String <<PK>>
  +title : String
  +course : String
  +semester : String
  +description : String
  +skills : String
  +source : Source
  +userId : String <<FK>>
}

class Resume {
  +id : String <<PK>>
  +title : String
  +date : String
  +userId : String <<FK>>
}

enum Source <<enumeration>> {
  Canvas
  Personal
}

User "1" ||--o{ "0..*" Project : owns
User "1" ||--o{ "0..*" Resume : owns
Project "0..*" }o--|| "1" Source : classified as

note right of Project::skills
  JSON-encoded string, e.g. ["React","SQL"].
  Prisma SQLite has no scalar lists; parsed to
  string[] at the API boundary. See
  docs/ai-design-review.md.
end note

note bottom of User
  Only id is fixed by the current schema task;
  username/createdAt land with server-side auth.
end note

@enduml
